WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.915
At the coffee cart, I watch the light across the street.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.300
[Traffic rises. A faint double tap.]

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.900
When it changes, I go.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.917
At the top of the steps, the brass door is open.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.400
Lucky, I think.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.338
In my notebook the whole trip fits on one line.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.400
Brooklyn. Then class.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.200
[Rail wheels, again.]

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.954
What did I put in the space between those words?

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.442
Same corner. Same light.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.500
[Two light taps, now clear.]

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.400
There it is again.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.847
A spoon touches the rim. Twice.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.400
[A spoon rings twice against a cup.]

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.869
There's another cup behind the one I took.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.639
The door hangs open for the length of a breath.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.054
Someone's hand is still on the other side.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.523
I remember the brass. I don't remember the hand.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.600
[A door hinge. A soft click.]

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.198
If you ask how long it takes to get here,

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.600
give me a minute.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:13.000
[Two taps in the distance.]
